## Original Content
China and India will hold the 25th round of talks between their special representatives on the boundary question in Beijing on Tuesday, the Chinese Foreign Ministry announced on Monday.

## Summary
China and India are set to hold the 25th round of talks on the boundary question in Beijing between their special representatives. The event was announced by the Chinese Foreign Ministry. This marks a continuation of diplomatic discussions on border issues.

## Key Points
- The 25th round of boundary talks between China and India is scheduled to occur.
- The talks will be held in Beijing, as announced by the Chinese Foreign Ministry.
- Discussions will involve special representatives from both countries.
- This event highlights ongoing diplomatic efforts to address the boundary question.


